course: dictionary
lesson: 11000
title: Washing: a word with two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning with the words around them. «Washing» is one of them. Look at the clues in the sentence before you decide what it means.
explain: «Hang out the washing before it rains.» The clothes are the clue: you hang out clothes, so washing means the clothes that need washing or have just been washed. «I am washing my hands» is different. The word «am» tells you it is happening now, so washing means cleaning.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If «washing» means cleaning and the sentence still works, you have the right meaning. In a Sydney home, a girl finds a sharp knife «in the washing-up», so the family now washes knives separately.
fact: Washing can mean cleaning something with water, often with soap.
fact: In the UK, Australia, New Zealand and Ireland, washing can mean the clothes that need washing or have just been washed.
fact: As part of the verb «wash», washing means cleaning now, as in «I am washing my hands».
fact: Washing hands with soap for about 20 seconds removes germs, especially before eating and after the toilet.
fact: «Washing-up» means washing the dishes, and «washing machine» means a machine that cleans clothes.
exercise: In «Hang out the washing before it rains», what does washing mean? | *The clothes that need washing or have just been washed | Dirty dishes waiting in the sink | A bowl of water for drinking | Cleaning your hands with soap right now
exercise: In «I am washing my hands before lunch», what does washing mean? | *Cleaning, and happening now | A soap bubble that bursts | Clothes waiting in a basket | The surface of a pond
exercise: Helping with the washing up is useful work at home. What is the washing up? | Hanging clothes on a line | Cleaning the car | Drying the floor | *Washing the dishes
test: In «Brightly coloured liquid capsules for washing machines have been mistaken for sweets», what is a washing machine? | A machine that makes soap bubbles for children | *A machine that cleans clothes with water | A kind of washing line | Sweets sold in a shop
test: «A drop of washing-up liquid weakens the skin so a resting paper clip sinks at once.» What does the liquid do to the water? | *Makes the water's surface weaker | Makes the water freeze | Makes the water sweet to taste | Turns the water hot
exam: In «Her washing is still wet on the line», what does washing mean? | *The clothes that have been washed | Cleaning with soap right now | A bowl for washing up | A thin cloth for dishes
